 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
--   **Overflow:** If more than 1023 points contribute to a pixel, the naive 18-18-18-10 bit pattern (used in HQS1×) overflows. The 16-16-16-16 pattern handles up to 255 points in the main buffer before falling back, with a safety margin of $65,536 - 256$ counts [S1].
--   **Simultaneous Accesses:** The unused $2^{16} - 256$ counts serve as a safety margin for potentially several thousand simultaneously executing threads to detect the overflow. If more or significantly fewer than 65k simultaneous accesses to a pixel are expected, the bit pattern may be changed accordingly [S1].
